    "q-320820": {
      "dom_id": "step-q320820",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)\\operatorname{log}⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n**Hint:** $\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)={log}_{10}⁡(x)$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x))}^{′}\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x){(\\operatorname{log}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({sec}^{2}⁡(x))(\\operatorname{log}⁡(x))+(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x))(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
